## Tutorials

The CSSobject-fitproperty is used to specify how an <img> or <video> should 
be resized to fit its container.

This property can take one of the following values:

Theobject-fit: fill;value does not preserve the aspect ratio, and the image is resized to fill the container (the 
image will be stretched or squeezed to fit):

Theobject-fit: cover;value preserves the aspect ratio, and 
the image fills the container. The image will be clipped to fit:

Theobject-fit: contain;value preserves the aspect ratio, and fits the image inside the container, without cutting - will leave empty 
space if needed:

Theobject-fit: none;value does not resize or scale the image:

Theobject-fit: scale-down;value scales the image down to the smallest version ofnoneorcontain:

Here we have two images and we want them to fill the width of 50% of the browser window and 100% of the height of the container.

In the following example we do NOT useobject-fit, so when we resize the browser window, the aspect ratio of the images will be destroyed:

In the next example, we useobject-fit: cover;, so when we resize the browser window, the aspect ratio of the images 
is preserved:

The following table lists the CSS object-* properties:

### Code Examples

```
.image-container {
width: 200px;
height: 300px;
border: 1px solid black;
margin-bottom: 25px;
}
.image-container img {
width: 100%;
height: 100%;
object-fit: fill;
}

---

.image-container {
width: 200px;
height: 300px;
border: 1px solid black;
margin-bottom: 25px;
}
.image-container img {
width: 100%;
height: 100%;
object-fit: cover;
}

---

.image-container {
width: 200px;
height: 300px;
border: 1px solid black;
margin-bottom: 25px;
}
.image-container img {
width: 100%;
height: 100%;
object-fit: contain;
}

---

.image-container {
width: 200px;
height: 300px;
border: 1px solid black;
margin-bottom: 25px;
}
.image-container img {
width: 100%;
height: 100%;
object-fit: none;
}

---

.image-container {
width: 200px;
height: 300px;
border: 1px solid black;
margin-bottom: 25px;
}
.image-container img {
width: 100%;
height: 100%;
object-fit: scale-down;
}
```

