## Tutorials

The CSSobject-positionproperty 
is used together with theobject-fitproperty to 
specify how an <img> or <video> should be positioned with x/y coordinates within 
its container.

The first value controls the x-axis and the second value controls the y-axis. 
The value can be a string (left, center or right), or a number (in px or %). 
Negative values are also allowed.

Let's say that the part of the image that is shown, is not the part that we 
want. To 
position the image, we will use theobject-positionproperty.

Here we position the image so that the great old building is in 
center:

Here we will use theobject-positionproperty 
to position the image so that the famous Eiffel Tower is in center:

The following table lists the CSS object-* properties:

### Code Examples

```
.image-container {
width: 200px;
height: 300px;
border: 1px solid black;
}
.image-container img {
width: 100%;
height: 100%;
object-fit: cover;
object-position: 80% 
  100%;
}

---

.image-container {
width: 200px;
height: 300px;
border: 1px solid black;
}
.image-container img {
width: 100%;
height: 100%;
object-fit: cover;
object-position: 15% 
  100%;
}
```

